msgid "Trimble PX-1 RTX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-trimble-px1.rst:8
#: 93e0488a3c6a4933a011dbecd10cc40b
msgid "The Trimble PX-1 RTX is a relatively expensive but also highly accurate RTX GNSS+INS. It supports corrections from a satellite or cellular network through `CenterPoint® RTX Correction service <https://positioningservices.trimble.com/en/rtx>`__. RTX provides centimeter accuracy without the use of a base station. Although the PX-1 is designed to be used as an external inertial navigation system, it is also supported for use as a strict GPS in ArduPilot. Detailed `information from the manufacturer can be found here <https://advancedairmobility.trimble.com/>`__."
msgstr ""

